As usual, let $a = BC,$ $b = AC,$ and $c = AB.$  From right triangle $AFC,$ $AF = b \cos A.$  By the Extended Law of Sines, $b = 2R \sin B,$ so
\[AF = 2R \cos A \sin B.\]From right triangle $ADB,$ $\angle DAB = 90^\circ - B.$  Then $\angle AHF = B,$ so
\[HF = \frac{AF}{\tan B} = \frac{2R \cos A \sin B}{\sin B/\cos B} = 2R \cos A \cos B = 6.\]Also from right triangle $AFC,$
\[CF = b \sin A = 2R \sin A \sin B = 21.\]Therefore,
\[\tan A \tan B = \frac{2R \sin A \sin B}{2R \cos A \cos B} = \frac{21}{6} = \boxed{\frac{7}{2}}.\]

With summation notation, $S = \sum_{i=1}^{2007} \sqrt{1 + \tfrac{1}{i^2} + \tfrac{1}{(i+1)^2}}$. By using a common denominator and simplifying, we have
\begin{align*} S &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} \sqrt{ \frac{i^2 (i^2 + 2i + 1) + i^2 + 2i + 1 + i^2}{i^2 (i+1)^2} } \\ &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} \sqrt{ \frac{i^4 + 2i^3 + 3i^2 + 2i + 1}{i^2 (i+1)^2} } \\ &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} \sqrt{ \frac{(i^2 + i + 1)^2}{i^2 (i+1)^2} } \\ &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} \frac{i^2 + i + 1}{i^2 + i} \\ &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} (1 + \frac{1}{i(i+1)}) \\ &= \sum_{i=1}^{2007} (1 + \frac{1}{i} - \frac{1}{i+1}) \end{align*}
Notice that part of the terms telescope, making calculation simpler. Calculation results in $S = 2007 + 1 - \tfrac{1}{2008}$. Thus, $S^2 = (2008 - \tfrac{1}{2008})^2 = 4032064 - 2 + (\tfrac{1}{2008})^2$. Since $0 < (\tfrac{1}{2008})^2 < 1$, we conclude that $\lfloor S^2\rfloor = \boxed{4032062}$.

The number of workers will be inversely proportional to the time needed to complete the job.  This means that the product $(\text{number of workers})\times(\text{days to complete job})$ will be a constant.  In this case, that constant will be: $$4\times 1.25=5$$ For three workers, the product will remain the same.  Let $D$ equal the number of days needed for three workers to complete the job.  Then, \begin{align*}
