solution:
Note that $(0,5)$ and $(1,2)$ are two points on the line, so the line has a direction vector of
\[\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.\][asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, P, V;

A = ((5 + 10)/3, -10);
B = ((5 - 10)/3, 10);
V = (-4,-2);
